# Environment / secrets
configs/*.env
# exception: the integration CI's configs are not secrets — they are throwaway
# presets for ephemeral runners, and they must live in the repository for the
# workflow to use them.
!configs/ci.env
# the nginx variant (B-V3-7): without it the `nginx` job would not find the file
# at checkout, and the config test would fail in CI too.
!configs/ci-nginx.env
# the second-instance variant (I4): same reason, and it would have been missed —
# the file was written, the job referenced it, and `git status` did not mention
# it because this very rule swallowed it. a clone would have had a job pointing
# at a file that is not there (the shape of A-V3-18).
!configs/ci-instance.env
docs/*.md

# Rust build artifacts
/target

# local clone of the GitHub wiki (a separate git repository)
/wiki
/CLAUDE.md